Z||000000||jfire||10-19-2001||10:53 AM||||I'm intrigued about the Ferrari-Fiero conversion, and was wondering...<BR>As I have no experience with kitcars, and cannot build one, Which Ferrari-Fiero would be a good one to look for, and where do I look to find one? Also, what price should I expect to pay for an average car? Also, what about the MERA car?<P>Any help would be appreciated.<P>Thank You.||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||11:04 AM||||Welcome to the forum... that's a pretty broad question.  If you're looking at purchasing a finished rebody... I've seen 4 cyl 308/328 conversions sell for $5-7K, with a V6 I've seen up to $16k (nice car) and with a V8 I've seen from $7-20K (many variables).  The MERA is a little more valuable than other rebodies- typically see them in Good condition for around $12-15k.  As for other body styles, I've seen F355's sell for anywhere from $8k (crap) to $45k (V8 and beautiful)averaging around $24k.  Same idea for the Testarossa/512TR & F40 conversions.  The F50 is probably a little more rare... never actually seen a completed one for sale before.  <P>Check/watch these types of places as well as Ebay:<BR> <A HREF="http://priceofhistoys.com/showroom/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://priceofhistoys.com/showroom/index.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.paulsexotics.com/showroom.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paulsexotics.com/showroom.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/2021/forsale.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/2021/forsale.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ck3.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ck3.com/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.kitcars.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kitcars.com/</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
